## Summary

A direct caller of the annotation library can receive an error saying a text box was left unchanged while its properties have already changed. For an unlocked text box with Chinese contents, an existing normal appearance and no undrawn marker, restyling returns AnnotError::Undrawable but retains the requested color, opacity and border width. Resizing the same input also returns an error after retaining the new rectangle. Both calls keep the original appearance, so a caller that retains the document after the error gets inconsistent annotation data.

## Steps to reproduce

1. At the baseline under Runtime or environment, save the following synthetic integration test as `crates/annot/tests/refused_edits.rs`. It creates a one-page PDF and attaches an indirect FreeText annotation whose Contents is 欢迎, whose existing appearance is a black vector drawing, and which has no locked flag or undrawn marker. The appearance does not need an embedded font to reach the refusal guard.

